    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32937" root="فتق" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْتَقٌ</span></b> , of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْعَلٌ</span>, (S, TA,) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفَتْقُ</span>
[“ the act of slitting ” &amp;c.], (TA,) <i>A carpenter.</i>
(S, O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>A</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَدَّاد</span> [which signifies a
<i>worker in iron:</i> but it also has the meaning here
next following, which may therefore be intended
by him who first gave this explanation of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْتَقٌ</span>].
(AZ, O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>A</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَوَّاب</span> [i. e. <i>door-keeper</i>].
(O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <i>A king.</i> (AZ, O, K.)

